# Round glmwire's timed term: GLM-5.3-Flash decode through the NextN MTP window (BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp) on the
# A6000, plan (a), prose ids, depth 512. Derivation [derived]: speed ratio = (1 + alpha) / (V2/S1 + D/S1), with
# S1 = 47.7 ms (the plain step, 20.95 tok/s), V2/S1 = 1.13-1.51 (docs/cards/glmpair-probe.card), D = 2.4-2.7 ms
# (layer 45: the card share, 874 MB of non-expert weights and the shared head, 1.29-1.42 ms plus launches; the host
# share, 8 routed experts of 15.2 MB, 0.9-1.0 ms), alpha = 26/38 = 0.684 (gate_glm5next_mtp (w), the set's
# 64-position prompt; ik 27/35 on the same set): 22.5-29.9 tok/s, centre 25.7. llama.cpp #27754's MTP arm read
# 23.29 tok/s on this card; beating it needs V2/S1 <= 1.46 at this alpha (1.54 at ik's). Layer 45's routed
# experts are in the load's host set, read in before the `fed` record, so the timed window takes no first-touch
# read of them. The variable reaches generate_glm5next through BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV: the runner's ours command
# inherits the environment (the reference arms ignore it).
kind: baseline
question: does GLM-5.3-Flash's NextN MTP window beat the plain step, and llama.cpp #27754's MTP arm, at depth 512?
term: tok/s(mean) @ n=96, depth 512, A6000: the ours arm under BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp, 1e3 over its SMOKE mean_ms (the
  kept positions' walls, each window's wall over the rows it kept), plan (a), prose ids
unit: tok/s
# Corrected 2026-10-01 with glmpair-probe.card's V2/S1 1.34-1.52 (was 1.13-1.51): ~~22.5..29.9~~ 22.4..25.3,
# center 23.6 tok/s at alpha 0.684 [derived]; llama.cpp #27754's MTP arm is 23.29, so the verdict sits in the band.
predict: 22.4..25.3
condition: one lease, 2 rounds; every ours row prints an mtp summary with proposals above 0, and its tokens line
  equals the plain run's of the same 512 ids (the functional run on the 3090 before the lease prints both; (w)
  holds it on the set); no row carries [cpu-busy], [other-busy] or [cold]; the lcpp27754mtp arm in the same lease;
  the full output to a file first. Command: BLOOMERY_DECODE_N=96 BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/glmwire-mtp.card BLOOMERY_DRAFT=mtp'
  just depth-gpu-glm5next 512 lcpp27754mtp:512 > <log> 2>&1
decide-in: land glmwire; the MTP row goes to rig-log beside the plain row; the accept-time chain overlap (the
  next window's row 0 under the chain, -1 to -2.5 ms [derived]) is the next lever
decide-below: take the V2/S1 probe (docs/cards/glmpair-probe.card) if it has not sat; if it has and sits in its
  band, one nsys of the drafted window (the verify's host legs and the chain's walk) before any lever
reason: the first timed number of GLM's MTP arm, the row the public table sets beside #27754's MTP arm; why
  now: the CLI arm exists and the NextN load's host set holds layer 45
decide-above: re-derive alpha at depth 512 on prose from the mtp summary's kept counts (0.684 is the set's
  64-position prompt) and raise the model's alpha before the next round
